ght interception.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rstb20070028f02"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Change in vegetation carbon predicted by the ED model (as placed in the IMOGEN modelling structure) for Amazonia (the same region as used in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig1">figure 1</xref>). The simulation is for a control climate based on the CRU climatology, with climate change anomalies based on HadCM3.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rstb20070028f03"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Spatial representation of vegetation carbon for the identical simulation with the ED model as given in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig3">figure 3</xref>. (<italic>a</italic>) The pre-industrial period and (<italic>b</italic>) centred on the last decade of the twenty-first century.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rstb20070028f04"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>